course: dictionary
lesson: 299
title: The giant snake of the rivers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Context means the words around a word. They often give you clues to its meaning. «Anacondas live mostly in swamps and slow rivers, where the water helps hold up their heavy bodies.» Swamps, rivers and water are the clues. An anaconda is a snake that lives in or near water.
explain: «Pythons, boas and anacondas are the giants of the snake world.» Giants is a clue that an anaconda is a very large snake. The green anaconda is so heavy that it is the heaviest snake in the world.
explain: A scientist checks a tale by measuring and testing. A tale is a story, and some stories about anacondas may not be true. «No anaconda over about seven metres has ever been well measured.» So the biggest stories are not proven yet.
fact: An anaconda is a very large snake from South America that lives in and near rivers and swamps.
fact: The green anaconda is the heaviest snake in the world.
fact: An anaconda is not venomous. It kills its prey by squeezing it until it cannot breathe, then swallows it whole.
fact: Anacondas give birth to live babies.
exercise: «Anacondas live mostly in swamps and slow rivers.» Where do anacondas mostly live? | *In swamps and slow rivers | In the snow | In dry deserts | On tall mountains
exercise: An anaconda is not venomous. What does this mean? | It can fly | It is very poisonous | It is green in colour | *It has no poison in its bite
exercise: «Pythons, boas and anacondas are the giants of the snake world.» Find and copy one word that means very large animals. | *giants | pythons | world | snake
test: In the rainforest food chain, what is a top predator? | *An animal that hunts other animals for food | A bird that cannot fly | A plant that grows in water | A fish that swims in rivers
test: «A scientist checks a tale by measuring and testing.» What does tale mean here? | A measuring tape | A river | *A story | A kind of food
exam: Which clue tells you that prey means animals an anaconda hunts for food? | *It swallows its prey whole | It lives in a swamp | It is green | It is a snake
